## Per-connection footprint

`bench-peer-scaling` measures the protocol core's per-connection cost (inline state plus
heap) for one more connection: idle, after a first message warms its read path, with
sixteen calls in flight, and as a loop-hosted connection that also carries a vat. It then
extrapolates each to half a million sessions. The footprint gate protects the warmed
number; the others are measured points, and the served connection sits a little above the
gate because it carries that vat. The extrapolation is straight-line arithmetic on
in-process core memory; pancake has not measured a node actually holding that many live
sockets. Measure your own: `zig build bench-peer-scaling -Doptimize=ReleaseFast`.

```=html
